            "fontId": "custom-99a2c890-1804-450c-8af8-6b60ee9a6b27",
            "fontSize": "28",
            "fontWeight": "400",
            "textDirection": "ltr",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontVariantId": "normal-400",
            "textDecoration": "none",
            "letterSpacing": "0",
            "fills": [
              {
                "fillColor": "#a3adbd",
                "fillOpacity": 1
              }
            ],
            "fontFamily": "Arimo"
          },
          {
            "lineHeight": "1.4",
            "fontStyle": "normal",
            "children": [
              {
                "lineHeight": "1.4",
                "fontStyle": "normal",
                "textTransform": "none",
                "textAlign": "left",
                "fontId": "custom-99a2c890-1804-450c-8af8-6b60ee9a6b27",
                "fontSize": "28",
                "fontWeight": "400",
                "textDirection": "ltr",
                "fontVariantId": "normal-400",
                "textDecoration": "none",
                "letterSpacing": "0",
                "fills": [
                  {
                    "fillColor": "#a3adbd",
                    "fillOpacity": 1
                  }
                ],
                "fontFamily": "Arimo",
                "text": "Ed's setup starts the new loop like Empty tracks, then names tracks 1 to 4 Guitar, Boom, RC20 and Vox and puts one Ed's Rack sound on each track: Acoustic Rhythm 1, Boom Dry, Bass Octave 1 and Vocal Close. The track names come from a published breakdown of Ed Sheeran's pedal; the sounds are our choice, not his settings, and the sheet does not claim otherwise. Each rack holds only the pedals its preset turns on, so the four fit the 96 kHz effects budget. The racks are heard on playback, as every track rack is, and no footswitch is bound. Inputs, outputs, All tracks, tracks 5 to 8, tempo and pedal setup stay as Empty tracks keeps them. The four new-loop tiles that get a sound are outlined."
              }
            ],
            "textTransform": "none",
            "textAlign": "left",
            "fontId": "custom-99a2c890-1804-450c-8af8-6b60ee9a6b27",
            "fontSize": "28",
            "fontWeight": "400",
            "textDirection": "ltr",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontVariantId": "normal-400",
